1
00:00:07,749 --> 00:00:11,772
In eastern Tibet, the
story goes, a master dies.

2
00:00:11,852 --> 00:00:14,748
The body is wrapped and
left in a small room.

3
00:00:14,828 --> 00:00:16,677
Over a week it grows smaller.

4
00:00:16,757 --> 00:00:18,796
Rainbows are seen over the house.

5
00:00:18,876 --> 00:00:22,877
When the room is opened, only
the hair and the nails are left.

6
00:00:23,702 --> 00:00:27,332
This is After Anatta. In
this video I only report.

7
00:00:27,412 --> 00:00:30,185
What the traditions say
the rainbow body is,

8
00:00:30,265 --> 00:00:33,391
how they say it is reached,
what the reports of it are,

9
00:00:33,471 --> 00:00:36,054
and where other traditions
tell something like it.

10
00:00:36,134 --> 00:00:37,879
I keep my own view out of it.

11
00:00:38,706 --> 00:00:41,711
Start with Dzogchen, the Great Perfection,

12
00:00:41,791 --> 00:00:44,582
taught in the Nyingma school and in Bön.

13
00:00:45,393 --> 00:00:48,940
Dzogchen speaks of the
basis in three aspects.

14
00:00:49,020 --> 00:00:52,758
Its essence is empty,
pure from the beginning.

15
00:00:52,838 --> 00:00:56,223
Its nature is clear,
spontaneously present.

16
00:00:56,303 --> 00:00:58,288
And its display never stops.

17
00:00:58,368 --> 00:01:02,256
The display first shows
as sound, light and rays,

18
00:01:02,336 --> 00:01:04,651
and the light as five lights.

19
00:01:05,474 --> 00:01:08,383
Then the texts tell how saṃsāra begins.

20
00:01:08,463 --> 00:01:12,595
When the display is not recognised
as the basis's own radiance,

21
00:01:12,675 --> 00:01:16,305
it is taken as something
other, standing over there.

22
00:01:16,385 --> 00:01:20,734
The five lights are grasped, and
they harden into the five elements,

23
00:01:20,814 --> 00:01:24,719
earth, water, fire, air and space.

24
00:01:24,809 --> 00:01:27,718
From the elements come
the body and the world.

25
00:01:27,798 --> 00:01:33,261
So, in Dzogchen's terms, the ordinary
body is light not recognised.

26
00:01:33,341 --> 00:01:37,559
The rainbow body is said to be the
same process run the other way.

27
00:01:38,382 --> 00:01:41,604
There are two practices. The
first is cutting through.

28
00:01:41,684 --> 00:01:47,134
The practitioner recognises rigpa, the
knowing that is empty and clear at once,

29
00:01:47,214 --> 00:01:51,414
and rests in it. This is said
to free the mind from grasping.

30
00:01:51,494 --> 00:01:53,710
The second is direct crossing.

31
00:01:53,790 --> 00:01:58,737
With particular postures and
gazes, lights appear in open space.

32
00:01:58,817 --> 00:02:00,358
Small drops of light.

33
00:02:00,461 --> 00:02:05,381
Fine threads. They grow into patterns,
and then into whole mandalas.

34
00:02:05,461 --> 00:02:07,079
These are the four visions.

35
00:02:07,159 --> 00:02:10,395
The fourth is called the
exhaustion of phenomena.

36
00:02:10,475 --> 00:02:15,544
At the fourth, the texts say,
nothing is grasped as solid any more,

37
00:02:15,624 --> 00:02:17,084
the body included.

38
00:02:17,914 --> 00:02:20,226
The texts also speak of lamps.

39
00:02:20,306 --> 00:02:22,182
One lamp is the eyes.

40
00:02:22,262 --> 00:02:25,592
Another is the open expanse
the lights appear in.

41
00:02:25,672 --> 00:02:28,337
Another is the circles
of light themselves.

42
00:02:28,417 --> 00:02:32,309
And the last is the wisdom that
knows them as its own display.

43
00:02:33,121 --> 00:02:35,418
Dzogchen names three results.

44
00:02:35,498 --> 00:02:39,467
Some teachers say that cutting through
alone leads at death to the body

45
00:02:39,547 --> 00:02:42,076
dissolving into tiny particles.

46
00:02:42,156 --> 00:02:46,397
The rainbow body comes when direct
crossing is completed at death.

47
00:02:46,477 --> 00:02:48,788
Over about a week the body shrinks.

48
00:02:48,868 --> 00:02:53,054
Sweet scents are reported, and
rainbows, and beams of light.

49
00:02:53,134 --> 00:02:56,003
In the end only hair and nails are left.

50
00:02:56,083 --> 00:03:00,310
And the rarest is the great
transference. There is no death at all.

51
00:03:00,390 --> 00:03:04,671
The body becomes a body of light
that can still act in the world.

52
00:03:04,751 --> 00:03:09,934
The tradition names Garab Dorje,
Padmasambhava and Vimalamitra.

53
00:03:10,757 --> 00:03:13,557
Teachers within Dzogchen add a warning.

54
00:03:13,637 --> 00:03:18,965
The shrinking body is what people see,
but it is not the rainbow body itself.

55
00:03:19,045 --> 00:03:21,940
The rainbow body is first a realization.

56
00:03:22,020 --> 00:03:25,052
When the fourth vision
is complete, everything,

57
00:03:25,132 --> 00:03:29,658
the body included, is seen as
the display of the five lights.

58
00:03:29,738 --> 00:03:33,190
The corpse is a sign of it,
and not always a sign at all.

59
00:03:33,270 --> 00:03:38,788
Malcolm Smith, a Dzogchen teacher, calls a
body that shrinks and disappears a partial

60
00:03:38,868 --> 00:03:43,326
rainbow body, a sign the fourth
vision was not fully finished.

61
00:03:43,406 --> 00:03:46,628
And control over the
elements, the teachers say,

62
00:03:46,708 --> 00:03:50,844
is a worldly power that yogis of
other traditions can gain too.

63
00:03:51,657 --> 00:03:54,281
Now the Gelug school of Tsongkhapa.

64
00:03:54,360 --> 00:03:59,376
Gelug does not teach direct crossing,
and it does not aim at a rainbow body.

65
00:03:59,456 --> 00:04:02,745
Its view is that nothing
exists from its own side,

66
00:04:02,825 --> 00:04:05,857
and everything works as
a dependent designation.

67
00:04:05,937 --> 00:04:09,471
The view alone, it says, ripens slowly.

68
00:04:09,551 --> 00:04:14,190
The fast path is tantra, because
tantra works with the subtle body.

69
00:04:14,989 --> 00:04:17,368
Gelug tantra rests on one point.

70
00:04:17,448 --> 00:04:21,104
Mind and wind are one
thing seen from two sides.

71
00:04:21,184 --> 00:04:25,710
At the subtlest level they are the very
subtle wind and the very subtle mind of

72
00:04:25,790 --> 00:04:28,822
clear light. Everyone meets this at death.

73
00:04:28,902 --> 00:04:33,210
The elements dissolve one into
the next, earth into water,

74
00:04:33,290 --> 00:04:38,265
water into fire, fire into
wind, wind into consciousness.

75
00:04:38,345 --> 00:04:42,151
Then come three appearances,
white, red and black.

76
00:04:42,231 --> 00:04:44,039
Then the clear light of death.

77
00:04:44,119 --> 00:04:49,112
Most beings do not recognise it, and
habit carries them on to a new birth.

78
00:04:49,926 --> 00:04:52,333
The yogi rehearses this while alive.

79
00:04:52,413 --> 00:04:56,721
The winds are drawn into the central
channel and dissolve at the heart.

80
00:04:56,801 --> 00:04:58,370
The clear light dawns.

81
00:04:58,459 --> 00:05:03,637
From the subtle wind that carried it, a
body of pure wind arises in the form of

82
00:05:03,717 --> 00:05:08,651
the deity. This is the illusory
body, separate from the coarse body,

83
00:05:08,731 --> 00:05:10,974
like a dream body but stable.

84
00:05:11,054 --> 00:05:14,384
When the clear light
realises emptiness directly,

85
00:05:14,464 --> 00:05:19,375
and the two are joined, Gelug calls
that union the body of a buddha.

86
00:05:20,194 --> 00:05:22,451
Why does it work, in Gelug's account?

87
00:05:22,531 --> 00:05:27,560
Because the body's material is
wind, and wind is one with mind.

88
00:05:27,640 --> 00:05:30,671
When the subtlest mind realises emptiness,

89
00:05:30,751 --> 00:05:34,095
the wind it rides on
arises as a pure body.

90
00:05:34,175 --> 00:05:36,269
And Gelug insists on one thing.

91
00:05:36,349 --> 00:05:39,041
The clear light must realise emptiness.

92
00:05:39,121 --> 00:05:43,651
Clarity alone, however deep,
is said to free nothing.

93
00:05:44,486 --> 00:05:47,029
The sign Gelug is known for is tukdam.

94
00:05:47,109 --> 00:05:50,493
After death a master is said
to rest in the clear light,

95
00:05:50,573 --> 00:05:55,425
sometimes for days, and the body
stays fresh. It does not shrink.

96
00:05:55,505 --> 00:06:01,227
In 2021, a team at the University of
Wisconsin measured thirteen such cases and

97
00:06:01,307 --> 00:06:03,958
found no detectable brain activity.

98
00:06:04,038 --> 00:06:06,702
They could only begin
about a day after death,

99
00:06:06,782 --> 00:06:10,126
and they tested the brain,
not the claim about the body.

100
00:06:10,206 --> 00:06:14,963
Tsongkhapa himself is said to have
become a buddha in the in-between state,

101
00:06:15,043 --> 00:06:16,879
through the illusory body.

102
00:06:16,959 --> 00:06:19,316
No rainbow body is claimed for him.

103
00:06:20,117 --> 00:06:22,673
A third system is the Kālacakra.

104
00:06:22,753 --> 00:06:26,001
In its night yoga, in a sealed dark room,

105
00:06:26,081 --> 00:06:29,412
and its day yoga, gazing at the open sky,

106
00:06:29,492 --> 00:06:35,492
ten signs appear in order. Smoke.
A mirage. A firefly. A lamp.

107
00:06:35,660 --> 00:06:40,866
A flame. The moon. The sun.
Darkness. A flash of lightning.

108
00:06:40,946 --> 00:06:42,754
And a great sphere of light.

109
00:06:42,834 --> 00:06:45,404
Its texts call what appears empty form.

110
00:06:45,484 --> 00:06:48,787
They say these images are
made of no atoms at all,

111
00:06:48,867 --> 00:06:51,531
and go beyond being and not being.

112
00:06:51,611 --> 00:06:55,947
They compare them to the image a
young girl sees in a divining mirror.

113
00:06:56,027 --> 00:06:59,480
Kālacakra's goal is not
called a rainbow body.

114
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:04,194
It speaks of a union of empty
form and unchanging bliss.

115
00:07:04,274 --> 00:07:08,026
The scholar Giacomella
Orofino shows that Longchenpa,

116
00:07:08,106 --> 00:07:13,461
the great Dzogchen writer, already set
these ten signs beside the four visions of

117
00:07:13,541 --> 00:07:15,028
direct crossing.

118
00:07:15,862 --> 00:07:19,736
Bön has its own Dzogchen,
its own lamps and visions,

119
00:07:19,816 --> 00:07:21,652
and its own rainbow body.

120
00:07:21,732 --> 00:07:25,320
One of its masters,
Shardza Tashi Gyaltsen,

121
00:07:25,400 --> 00:07:28,269
is said to have attained
it in nineteen thirty-four.

122
00:07:28,349 --> 00:07:32,875
Bön also has practices that Buddhism
does not frame the same way,

123
00:07:32,955 --> 00:07:35,243
such as offerings to the four guests.

124
00:07:36,061 --> 00:07:38,155
Even the tables of colours differ.

125
00:07:38,235 --> 00:07:41,674
Which element goes with
which buddha, which wisdom,

126
00:07:41,754 --> 00:07:46,542
which affliction: these change from
text to text, and from school to school.

127
00:07:47,345 --> 00:07:48,637
Now the reports.

128
00:07:48,717 --> 00:07:53,311
The modern cases often told are
Sonam Namgyal in nineteen fifty-two,

129
00:07:53,391 --> 00:07:56,372
and Khenpo A Chö in nineteen ninety-eight.

130
00:07:56,502 --> 00:08:01,776
For Khenpo A Chö, a local press report
said the body shrank to the size of a

131
00:08:01,856 --> 00:08:06,884
bean. A priest and scholar,
Francis Tiso, went to look into it.

132
00:08:06,964 --> 00:08:10,082
What he could gather was what
people had seen and told.

133
00:08:10,906 --> 00:08:13,829
Some popular papers call such cases proof,

134
00:08:13,909 --> 00:08:16,356
verified by hundreds of witnesses.

135
00:08:16,436 --> 00:08:18,218
They are eyewitness reports.

136
00:08:18,298 --> 00:08:22,307
None has been checked by anyone
independent. And the lists vary.

137
00:08:22,387 --> 00:08:25,405
A master whose body was ordinary at death,

138
00:08:25,485 --> 00:08:28,815
and whose relics were
kept, appears on one list.

139
00:08:28,895 --> 00:08:33,693
Another master's death is dated to one
year in one source and seventeen years

140
00:08:33,773 --> 00:08:35,242
later in another.

141
00:08:35,322 --> 00:08:40,079
The sixteenth Karmapa is listed too,
though what was reported after his death

142
00:08:40,159 --> 00:08:42,910
was tukdam, not a rainbow body.

143
00:08:43,729 --> 00:08:46,991
Buddhism is not alone in
telling of such a body.

144
00:08:47,071 --> 00:08:52,358
In Taoist inner alchemy, the
practitioner refines essence into energy,

145
00:08:52,438 --> 00:08:56,556
energy into spirit, and
spirit back into emptiness.

146
00:08:56,636 --> 00:09:02,127
The aim is the yang spirit, a body outside
the body that others can see and that can

147
00:09:02,207 --> 00:09:03,513
act in the world.

148
00:09:03,593 --> 00:09:08,662
A spirit body made by cultivating the
mind alone is called the yin spirit,

149
00:09:08,742 --> 00:09:10,891
seen only by oneself.

150
00:09:10,971 --> 00:09:15,388
Mind alone, they say, is not
enough. Two endings are told.

151
00:09:15,468 --> 00:09:18,594
In one, the body vanishes from the coffin,

152
00:09:18,674 --> 00:09:21,488
leaving only clothes or a staff.

153
00:09:21,568 --> 00:09:26,180
In the other, the master rises
in broad daylight, without dying.

154
00:09:26,994 --> 00:09:29,822
The Chan tradition tells
a story about this.

155
00:09:29,902 --> 00:09:34,985
The Taoist immortal Lü Dongbin visits the
Chan master Huanglong and speaks of his

156
00:09:35,065 --> 00:09:36,955
medicine of long life.

157
00:09:37,035 --> 00:09:39,686
Huanglong calls him a
corpse-guarding ghost.

158
00:09:39,766 --> 00:09:43,354
Even if you last eighty
thousand aeons, he says,

159
00:09:43,434 --> 00:09:46,262
in the end you fall into empty ruin.

160
00:09:46,342 --> 00:09:48,875
In the Chan telling, Lü then wakes up.

161
00:09:49,689 --> 00:09:51,035
Others tell of it too.

162
00:09:51,115 --> 00:09:55,967
In India, the Tamil saint Ramalinga
Swamigal went into his room in eighteen

163
00:09:56,047 --> 00:09:59,120
seventy-four and asked
that no one open it.

164
00:09:59,200 --> 00:10:01,742
When it was opened, he was not found.

165
00:10:01,822 --> 00:10:06,660
Eastern Orthodox monks speak of
the uncreated light of Mount Tabor.

166
00:10:06,740 --> 00:10:09,079
Sufis speak of a man of light.

167
00:10:09,159 --> 00:10:12,435
Each tradition reads the
result in its own way:

168
00:10:12,515 --> 00:10:15,886
a soul that survives,
a source to return to,

169
00:10:15,966 --> 00:10:19,831
a self made perfect, or a
light one comes to share.

170
00:10:20,629 --> 00:10:25,132
And the early Buddhist discourses have
their own way of placing such powers.

171
00:10:25,248 --> 00:10:29,489
Five of the six higher knowledges,
the bodily wonders among them,

172
00:10:29,569 --> 00:10:31,975
are shared with those
outside the teaching.

173
00:10:32,055 --> 00:10:36,205
Only the sixth, the ending of
the taints, is said to free.

174
00:10:37,038 --> 00:10:40,668
There is a Tibetan image worth
keeping. Raw leather is stiff.

175
00:10:40,748 --> 00:10:44,513
Rub butter into it under
the sun, and it grows soft.

176
00:10:44,593 --> 00:10:47,325
But a leather bag used
only to store butter,

177
00:10:47,405 --> 00:10:50,559
year after year, slowly hardens like wood.

178
00:10:50,639 --> 00:10:52,814
Then no butter will soften it again.

179
00:10:52,894 --> 00:10:57,642
Knowledge never worked into practice,
the saying goes, does the same.

180
00:10:58,474 --> 00:11:04,209
One ordinary moment helps me see why the
traditions speak this way. Hold an apple.

181
00:11:04,289 --> 00:11:08,517
The hardness. The coolness.
The red. The sweetness.

182
00:11:08,597 --> 00:11:10,786
Each appears as its conditions meet.

183
00:11:10,866 --> 00:11:14,767
Then a habit ties them into
one solid thing, out there.

184
00:11:14,847 --> 00:11:17,742
Untie that knot, and nothing is lost.

185
00:11:17,822 --> 00:11:22,217
Just this hardness, this
red, this sweetness, vivid.

186
00:11:23,044 --> 00:11:27,420
From a non-substantialist view, the
rainbow body is not difficult to

187
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:32,275
understand. But as this is my personal
view, I shall not comment here.

